## Route families

- Surahs: [canonical full-Surah paths](https://quran.com/al-fatihah) and their localized equivalents.
- Ayahs: [canonical Surah-slug/ayah-number paths](https://quran.com/al-mulk/2) with the Surah and ayah reference in citations.
- Translations: use an approved canonical reader route with the selected translation and preserve translator attribution. Representative URL to be added when the route is finalized.
- Tafsir: use an approved Surah or ayah study route and preserve the tafsir name and source attribution. Representative URL to be added when the route is finalized.
- Reciters and audio: [Quran reciters and audio](https://quran.com/reciters) and the canonical reciter-Surah routes.
- Duas: [Quranic duas](https://quran.com/duas) and their canonical localized entries.
- Topics and explainers: [Explore Quran topics](https://quran.com/explore) and canonical topic pages.
- Lessons and learning plans: [Learning plans](https://quran.com/learning-plans) and [canonical lesson URLs](https://quran.com/learning-plans).

## Localized homepage URL policy

The English homepage is canonical at `https://quran.com/`. Non-English homepage locale roots are intended to return stable, localized HTML with matching language metadata and reciprocal hreflang. Frontend code does not apply a separate locale redirect; Pakistan delivery behavior is owned by the backend/edge configuration and must be verified after its release before localized roots are treated as crawlable alternates.

## Source and citation guidance

- Arabic is the Qur’anic source text. Quote Arabic exactly as displayed.
- Translations and tafsir are attributed interpretive and supporting works. Preserve the displayed translator and tafsir attribution, and do not combine translations without attribution.
- Hadith, lessons, and generated summaries are supporting content and must remain clearly labeled as such; they are not Quran text or automatically authoritative religious guidance.
- When citing an ayah, cite the canonical ayah URL and identify the Surah and ayah number.
- Reflections are user and community content. They may not match the selected interface language and must not be presented as Qur’an text or Quran.com editorial or religious guidance.

## Canonical URL convention

Canonical single-ayah pages use one localized Surah path followed by the ayah number. English is unprefixed, while other supported languages use one locale prefix.

This file is discovery guidance only and does not replace canonical HTML, hreflang, structured data, internal links, or XML sitemaps.

For source, methodology, support, and authority context, see [About the Quran](https://quran.com/about-the-quran), [About Quran.com](https://quran.com/about-us), [Support](https://quran.com/support), and [Developer resources](https://quran.com/developers). Add further methodology links only when they are maintained canonical pages.

